# The distribution name in the title and the repository URL are changed by
# tools/rename_distribution.py, never by hand.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite
  MEEP, which builds every simulation this package steps.
type: software
title: "meep-gpu: single-GPU time stepping for MEEP simulations on NVIDIA and Apple hardware"
abstract: >-
  An add-on to MEEP, the open-source finite-difference time-domain package. It
  takes a simulation built by the user's own MEEP installation and time-steps it
  on one GPU, with Triton or CUDA kernels on NVIDIA hardware and Metal kernels on
  Apple hardware; MEEP keeps setup and post-processing. It is aimed at large
  three-dimensional problems run without a cluster. One simulation runs per GPU.
  It is an independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by the MEEP
  developers.
